-- title:
--   Constants of A=A₀[ζ_q] lie in the classifying map's image
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity such that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb C$ carries $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb Q\to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ for the subgroup $H=$ kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ whose maximal ideal contains $q$, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, and let $j\in K$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent series is the image of the $j$-series `jq`. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal $(q)$ and finite residue field, mapping to $A$ and to $K$ compatibly, containing a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity, with $\ell$ and $M'$ invertible in $A_0$. Assume: stability under variable change of level-$\ell$ structures `IsLevelPStructure` and of the kernel-polynomial predicates `IsGamma0PowAt` over all $A_0$-algebras; group laws $\mathcal G$ on the projective Weierstrass models of curves with unit discriminant that are chord–tangent and have the origin as identity; a level transport $\mathcal T$ for Drinfeld bases of level $q$ compatible with the two sections; and the two families `hVC`, `hCO` providing graded ring homomorphisms of projective coordinate rings realising variable changes and coefficient changes, with the stated inclusion of irrelevant ideals. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the moduli datum of `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ M' q …`, whose points over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ are Weierstrass curves over $T$ with unit discriminant equipped with a $\Gamma_0$-type kernel polynomial for each prime factor of $M'$, a level-$\ell$ structure and a Drinfeld basis of level $q$, taken up to variable change, with $j$-invariant as the $j$-function; thus $B_0$ is an $A_0$-algebra, of finite type, carrying a universal point through which every point factors uniquely. Let $x$ be a point over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has Laurent series `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`. If $\zeta_A\in A$ satisfies $\zeta_A^q=1$ and $A_0[\zeta_A]=A$, then for every $a\in A$ there is $b\in B_0$ whose image under the unique $A_0$-algebra map $B_0\to K$ classifying $x$ equals the image of $a$ in $K$.
--
--   The assertion is that, over an unramified base $A_0$ with finite residue field whose extension $A$ is generated by a $q$-th root of unity, the classifying homomorphism of the Tate point of the rigid full-level moduli problem has image containing all constants from $A$. It is used in the identification of the adic completion of the stalk of the moduli ring at the Tate point, including its level automorphisms.
